40,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"It appears the room is being used disproportionately by a few people, and the lack of cleanliness is becoming a systemic issue. The bins are being emptied daily because people are eating at their desks.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It seems we have lost a space for genuine connection. I found that our only unplanned interactions now happen by the printer, and difficult conversations are forced into the open, leaving a lingering silence.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,May,,"It's a total time sink! People are spending nearly half an hour just to get a hot lunch, and the facilities logs show we're constantly calling for help in the equipment rooms. We're bleeding hours!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The financial bleed is even worse than I thought. We've wasted 68,000 yen on tiny outside rentals because this room fails us. Plus, the fit-out quotes are steep—either 141,000 for a tech setup or 96,000 for a kitchen.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is revealing that the wall is but a thin veil, allowing every word to drift into our workspace. Furthermore, the fridge showed us that some carry the burden of cleaning while others simply forget.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Servas, that confirms my suspicion. The cleaning burden isn't shared equally, and the usage data shows only two people are utilizing the room frequently. We are dealing with a lack of accountability.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, accountability is important, but perhaps the lack of care stems from a lack of belonging. If we have no place to speak privately or bond, the room becomes just a utility, not a shared space.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, belonging is great, but it doesn't get the bins emptied or the lunch run shortened! If we turn this into a ""bonding"" space, who's going to spend their free time maintaining it? I'm not volunteering!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your fear of chores is touching, but let's focus on the actual cost. We're paying for outside rentals because we lack a functional space. Whether it's a kitchen or a meeting room, we need a return on investment.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Servas,,"We must remember that a room is not merely an investment or a utility, but a sanctuary for the mind. If the walls cannot hold a secret, the spirit cannot find true rest.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, a return on investment is only possible if the room is managed properly. If we invest in a fit-out without a system for cleaning and scheduling, we are just paying to create a more expensive mess.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Ryuji, I agree that management is key. However, if we only focus on the mess, we ignore the fact that we've become strangers. A space that allows for quiet, private dialogue might actually encourage more respect for the room.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,May,,"@Jonathan, a ""sanctuary"" sounds lovely until someone spills coffee on the rug and we're all arguing over whose turn it is to scrub it. Why do we always assume ""respect"" just happens magically?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, ""respect"" doesn't pay the bills or stop the bleeding of 68,000 yen. We're paying for external rooms because this one is useless. Let's stop the poetry and decide which investment actually solves the problem.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Servas,,"My dear friends, let us not let the numbers harden our hearts. While the cost is real, the cost of a restless spirit is far higher. We must find a balance between utility and peace.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,We cannot balance utility and peace if the basic rules of usage are ignored. The data shows a clear imbalance in both use and maintenance. Any decision we make must include a formal system for scheduling and cleaning.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I understand the need for rules, Ryuji, but a formal system cannot replace the need for a space where we can actually speak to one another. We are working side by side yet remaining strangers.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm with Ryuji on the rules, but let's be real: ""formal systems"" usually just mean one person ends up doing everything. If we're spending 25 minutes on lunch, we need a solution that saves time, not adds chores!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"You're all circling the same drain. Whether it's ""spirit"" or ""chores,"" the fact remains that we're paying a premium for outside rooms because this one is a failure. Let's just pick the option that stops the waste.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Let us breathe and remember that we are a team. Whether we seek to save yen or save time, we must ensure the room does not become a source of noise and stress for those of us working beside it.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
